Blastem for OSK---------------INTRODUCTION        Blastem is an XModem and Ymodem transfer program for OSK.  Iwrote this when I first got my MM/1, since I did not have access to an X/Ymodem transfer program at that time.        Blastem is simple to use.  Blastem -? gives the followingouput:        Syntax: Blastem [<opts>] {<filename> [<opts>]}        Function: Xmodem/Ymodem file transfer utility        Options:                -y        use YModem (Batch) protocol (XModem default)                -r        receive file(s) (default)                -s        send file(s)                -f        remove filler at EOF                -k        do not use 1K blocks (128 byte)                -l        checknum (8-bit)                -m        CRC (16-bit) (default)                -h        CRC (32-bit)                -t        use standard paths for transfer                -q        quiet (suppress messages)                -p=<path> modem path ('/t0' default)                -b=<size> buffer size (2K default)                -x        look in execution directory for file(s)                -z        get file names from standard input                -z=<path> get list of files from <path>        Most of this is self explanitory.  The only option that is a bit strange is -h, which selects 32-bit CRC checking.  This is an non-standardaddition to the X/Ymodem protocol, so the only way to use this is to anothermachine running Blastem.SOURCE CODE RULES        OK, now the rules:        1) You can modify the code as much as you want.        2) All original code must be distributed with your modifications.        3) You cannot make money from this distribution (unless it is part           of an archive).        4) If you use any of the source in your programms, then:           o You must distrubute your program with it's complete source             code.           o You cannot sell or rent your program or charge for it's use.        Have